# BeamNG integration checklist

This project is a prototype scaffold. To make it truly usable in BeamNG, follow this checklist.

## 1. Prepare the BeamNG mod structure
- Copy the `src/beamng_ets2_core` folder into your BeamNG mod environment.
- Ensure the Lua runtime can resolve the module path.
- Confirm your mod loader is enabled.

## 2. Add real assets
- Add or create actual truck model files.
- Add map assets if using custom maps.
- Add HUD or UI assets for your minimap and menu.

## 3. Wire to BeamNG runtime
- Use the BeamNG Lua API to load a map.
- Use the API to spawn a vehicle.
- Read player position and rotation from the active scene.

## 4. Build the actual menu
- Create a menu screen in the BeamNG UI system.
- Add truck cards or buttons.
- Add a map selection screen.

## 5. Build the minimap HUD
- Track the player vehicle position in world space.
- Convert world coordinates to minimap space.
- Add markers for destination, route, and vehicle.

## 6. Test in-game
- Launch BeamNG.
- Load the mod.
- Pick a truck and map.
- Spawn the vehicle.
- Drive and confirm the minimap updates.

## Notes

This file is intentionally a practical checklist rather than a claim that the prototype is complete. The real in-game integration still depends on BeamNG’s actual mod tools, APIs, and assets.
